From: ScorchDroid <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] android: carry the weapon's camera shake on the explosion event

Upstream ends Explosion's client body with
MainCamera::instance()->getCamera().addShake(params_->getShake()), which this
build does not compile - the camera here belongs to the renderer under
porting/, not to a MainCamera singleton. So the value travels with the
explosion instead of being a call.

Its own field rather than the existing `value`, which explosions already
spend on patch 0019's splash flag.

Zero for nearly every weapon: only Nuke, Baby Nuke, Death's Head and Funky
Bomb set <explosionshake> in the shipped mod, so this is inert for ordinary
fire. No game logic - the accumulation, the cap at 5 and the decay are all on
the renderer's side.

---
diff --git a/src/common/actions/Explosion.cpp b/src/common/actions/Explosion.cpp
--- a/src/common/actions/Explosion.cpp
+++ b/src/common/actions/Explosion.cpp
@@ -100,6 +100,11 @@
 		// splash sound, in the client body below). The renderer decides if
 		// the blast is actually under the water, as Water::explosion does.
 		effect.value = params_->getCreateSplash() ? 1.0f : 0.0f;
+		// V10: how hard this blast shakes the camera. Upstream calls
+		// MainCamera's addShake with it at the end of this same client body;
+		// here the camera belongs to the renderer, so the value travels with
+		// the explosion rather than as a call.
+		effect.shake = params_->getShake().asFloat();
 		// V1: what the client body's emitters would draw with - the
 		// weapon's texture set and whether it animates, the particle life
 		// range, additive or not (<luminance>), wind, and the explosion
